 the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and June to July, October to November and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 161% of normal in May to June but just 44% in July to August and 44% in November to December. Every grid here had its driest year in 1954, with grid 17259 at 64%.</p>"}
